# Review: MagazinePlugin

The plugin works, but the code has moved well past this spec. Feed sync, magazine curation, the
masonry article, the Post companion and the Magazine skill all exist. Their data model and curation
flow are different from what the spec says:

- **Data model.** `Feed` is `Subscription`. `Post` is an immutable queue entry with none of the four
  additions: `readAt` lives in `Subscription.postState`, curated `snippet` and `imageUrl` in
  `Magazine.postState`, fetched bodies in `PostContent` entries, and star and archive tags in a
  `TagIndex`.
- **Magazine.** `Magazine` holds an `Instructions` ref created eagerly by `Magazine.make`, not a
  lazily created `routine` with a `topic` field. It adds `postState` and `keep`.
- **Curation.** `CurateMagazine` is not deterministic. It syncs the feeds itself, runs the agent
  through `RunInstructions`, applies the agent's `completeJob` selection mechanically, and bounds the
  list by `keep` (starred first, then newest by `published`). `ListCandidatePosts` is an internal
  helper and `AddPostToMagazine` does not exist.

Solid and tested: `SyncFeed` dedup (`sync-feed.test.ts`), the end-to-end `CurateMagazine` run with a
scripted agent, the keep bound, candidate exclusion, article extraction and per-post atoms. The UI
stories that drive the Curate flow carry `!test`, so no automated test covers the toolbar, tiles,
read state or the companion.

Of 69 items: 2 done, 21 untested, 9 partial, 23 diverged, 14 missing. The spec should be rewritten
around `Subscription`, per-object state maps and agent-driven `CurateMagazine`.

